  "claim": "Source-backed oneshot lifecycle correction kept a fresh isolated Hindsight backend healthy after helper completion and repeat start; production native health checks remain enabled. Codex accepted the supported Hindsight MCP timeout setting.",
  "limitations": [
    "These are local integration checks of native lifecycle, using a disposable backend configured with provider none; no unchanged upstream test or model-quality comparison is claimed.",
    "Default cgroup cleanup reproduced an unavailable backend after native start exit zero. The corrected helper intentionally leaves detached backend lifecycle to the native profile manager; systemd generally discourages process mode for daemons it owns.",
    "The isolated repeat was an explicit native service start. Production timer active/waiting was observed; physical-host reboot and forced unhealthy recovery were not tested here.",
    "Codex per-server timeout is set to 360 seconds. A caller-supplied shorter deadline still wins, and no new model retrieval was run after this setting.",
    "Model/provider usage and monetary cost were not collected for this lifecycle check. Native Pg0 stop uses a nonchecking SDK wrapper; independent absence of both fixture listeners is the cleanup observation."
  ],
